      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is pretty \"normal\" and has been a thing since at least 2017.\nThe conditions are the height of your HMD in your playspace and probably the crouch animation(?).\nThe lower you go while you are in crouch space(Crouch animation plays on your avatar) the less you'll be able to tilt your head up.\nIm guessing it has something to do with the IK constraints of the neck/Head and the seamless transition between each of the 3 idle animations(Standing, Crouching, Prone). After all the closer you get to prone space the more forward leaning your upper body becomes while crouched, therefore the head cannot rotate that far to look towards the sky due to IK Constraints while playing said animation.\nThats my guess at least.\nHonestly makes me wonder if changing the prone and crouch animation to something where your chest stays straight and the IK has more freedom to move your neck accordingly would fix that.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-17T23:08:07.879Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If certain conditions are met, avatars cannot raise their heads higher than the front, even if they look up on the HMD.\nSneak motion & Avater 2.0 avatars & HMD use & no tracker\nIt doesn't seem to happen for people using desktop mode or trackers.",
